			"widgets_values":[
				"integrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action macro nature cinematography with soft natural light, a warm color palette, shallow depth of field, and delicate photorealistic detail. At sunset in a spring garden, the sky glows orange and pink above flower beds filled with colorful blossoms. A high-angle wide shot looks down on a fluffy white kitten with bright blue eyes and a red collar carrying a small golden bell. Among the flowers, the kitten notices a butterfly whose wings display vivid yellow, blue, and black patterns. Its ears immediately stand upright, its body becomes still, and its blue eyes remain intensely fixed on the butterfly as it lands on a nearby flower.\n\n[Shot 2] At 00:02.500, the camera cuts to an extreme close-up at flower level. The kitten lowers its chest slightly while keeping its hind legs ready beneath its body. One soft white front paw slowly lifts above the leaves, poised to pounce. Its whiskers angle forward, its pupils widen, and the red collar bell makes one faint metallic chime. In the blurred foreground, the butterfly opens and closes its patterned wings before suddenly taking flight.\n\n[Shot 3] At 00:04.200, the camera cuts to a low tracking shot moving rapidly alongside the kitten. The kitten springs forward and runs through the flower bed, maintaining the same fluffy white fur, blue eyes, and red bell collar. Its raised paws brush through petals and bend slender flower stems as it playfully chases the butterfly without catching or harming it. The butterfly flutters in quick curved paths between the flowers, its yellow, blue, and black wings flashing in the warm sunset light. The camera follows both subjects closely through the blossoms as drifting petals and tiny pollen particles glow in the backlight. Near the end, the butterfly rises just beyond the kitten's reach while the kitten makes one small playful leap and lands softly among the flowers.\n\noverall_soundscape: Gentle evening wind moves through leaves and flower stems, accompanied by soft bird calls and faint insect ambience. The kitten's paws rustle through the plants while its red collar bell rings in a quick, clear rhythm during the chase.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: Light pizzicato strings and soft wooden percussion at a playful moderate tempo, remaining delicate beneath the natural garden sounds and ending with a short upward flourish as the butterfly escapes.",
